Z||000001||Archie||11-15-2001||08:09 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Earl:<BR><B>  Hey Arch ,do you think you could modify your water pump drive to fit the 4cyl altinator? To stop the problem with it slipping.<BR>  It is driving me stark raving mad!!!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I don't know what you mean.... the W/P drive is a seperate unit from the Alternator drive.<P>I going to assume that you are talking about the "V" belt & that it is slipping on the Alt. pully. I'll also assume that you have already checked that the Alt. is in good shape and that the slipping is in fact caused by the Alt. pulley. If that is the case then all you need to do is change the pulley on the Alt. to one that is the correct width.<P>I'm really just guessing here because I need more info before I can make good suggestions.<P>To be honest, I don't recognize your EMail address etc. so I don't even know your name and I can't even look up your folder to see exactly what items you are using.<P>If you get a chance, call me at the shop today if you can 800-891-3608 & we'll figure out what the deal is.<P>Archie||||reg||1
